  fact-check: The reel_script says the Kumily buses are 'for' Sabarimala devotees and describes them as a service started for this purpose; the article only says buses run for devotees' convenience, which is roughly consistent, but the reel_script's claim that the buses 'செல்கின்றன' from Kovil Vazhi stand is fine; however the reel_script omits the key fact that Kovai-to-Pampa direct travel and group hire buses are offered as alternatives, which is partly present, so no omission here.
  fact-check: The slides_spec headline line hl1 says 'திருப்பூரில் இருந்து குமுளிக்கு பஸ்' and the slide 'முன்பதிவு' line says 'குழு பயணத்துக்கு வாடகை அரசு பஸ் ஏற்பாடு' which is acceptable, but the slide 'நேரம், கட்டணம்' line 'மண்டல பூஜை தொடங்கியுள்ள நிலையில் சேவை' adds a causal link (service started because of the puja) not stated in the article.
  fact-check: The reel_script says 'டி என் எஸ் டி சி இணையதளம்' while the article gives the website www.tnstc.in; the spelling of the agency name is a transliteration not in the article, and the website address is not mentioned in the reel_script.
  fact-check: The reel_script states the bus fare is per passenger and the times are given, both correct; but the slides_spec 'முன்பதிவு' slide states 'கோவையில் இருந்து பம்பைக்கு நேரடிப் பயணம்' under the booking heading, mixing the Kovai direct-travel fact with the booking fact into one slide without the article linking them that way.
